<title>USA: Golden State buying CENFED financial.</title>
<headline>Golden State buying CENFED financial.</headline>
<dateline>GLENDALE, Calif. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Golden State Bancorp Inc, the  parent company of Glendale Federal Bank, said Monday that it was purchasing CENFED Financial Corp, parent company of CenFed Bank, for $210 million in stock.</p>
<p>Golden State said the deal will be immediately accretive to its earnings, once it closes in early 1998. However, the bank said it expects to record pre-tax charges of approximately $30 million in conjunction with the merger.</p>
</text>
